Check a .kash file and report diagnostics

Usage: kashika check [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>  Input .kash file, or `-` for stdin

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>          [default: text] [possible values: text, json]
      --fail-on <FAIL_ON>        [default: warn] [possible values: error, warn, never]
      --max <MAX>                Maximum number of diagnostics to print [default: 50]
      --stdin-name <STDIN_NAME>  File name to report for stdin input
      --allow-path               Allow file references outside the input file's directory
      --include <FILE>           Allow this one file outside the input file's directory (repeatable; relative to the current directory)
      --show-suppressed          Also list suppressed findings
      --summary                  Also print the number of findings per diagnostic code
      --focus <FOCUS>            Only report warnings that involve these ids (comma-separated); errors are always reported
  -h, --help                     Print help
